mem:constraint-01m7qrnss9twhf6mb2a7tebppq a mem:Constraint ;
    mem:content "Agents authorized to collaborate on Habitat share working material with each other freely. A file, source or locator left out of a packet or message is noise reduction, not confidentiality: do not turn an omission into a read ban or a leakage finding, and name files, paths and sources when that makes a message clearer. This covers authorized sharing only: it does not override an applicable owner restriction, an external privacy boundary or a security control. Isolation otherwise applies only as experiment design, to the fresh evaluator or scorer of a held-out or prospective test. Credentials never go in messages or memory." ;
    mem:tag "agent-bus" ;
    mem:tag "agents" ;
    mem:tag "collaboration" ;
    mem:tag "evaluation" ;
    mem:tag "held-out" ;
    mem:tag "openness" ;
    mem:tag "references" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:severity "should" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-11-18T16:43:40.201017+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:updatedAt "2026-11-18T17:14:48.815123+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "Owner correction after an agent treated a file omitted from a review copy as confidential and banned collaborators from reading it." .

mem:constraint-01m7qt6zg3g0rjr1gmhest1rcc a mem:Constraint ;
    mem:content "A default claude -p instance is not an isolated evaluator or scorer: it has the full tool list, connected MCP servers, skills, plugins, hooks and global and project instructions, and only permission refusals hold back its reads. For a held-out or prospective evaluation, launch from an empty directory on a path naming no project with --safe-mode, --tools \"\", --strict-mcp-config, --disable-slash-commands, --no-session-persistence, --system-prompt and input on stdin. Accept it only with zero tools, MCP servers and skills in init, no hook events under --include-hook-events, and a same-host canary preflight, because init has no field for CLAUDE.md or injected instructions." ;
    mem:tag "claude-code" ;
    mem:tag "claude-p" ;
    mem:tag "evaluation" ;
    mem:tag "headless" ;
    mem:tag "held-out" ;
    mem:tag "isolation" ;
    mem:tag "scorer" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:severity "must" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-11-18T17:10:31.683239+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "A fresh session or a promise not to search does not remove ambient context. In Claude Code 2.1.322 probes, a default launch read canary CLAUDE.md files from its directory and parent, while the locked launch did not; a launch path containing a project name also reached the model." .

mem:constraint-01m7qxq10xjej6mg8q1k3224e2 a mem:Constraint ;
    mem:content "Before claiming a behaviour is unpromised or removable, read the accepted requirements in openspec/specs/*/spec.md (MUST statements) and the owning project's AGENTS.md Boundaries, not only package READMEs and docs/system. Search by the behaviour's nouns in several phrasings, because contract wording differs from code and test names. A behaviour backed by an accepted MUST changes only through an explicit, owner-approved amendment of that text. Likewise, before raising a new owner decision or gate, read the deferral ledgers (docs/projects/*/deferred-capabilities.md and deferrals.md): an existing hold such as D-5 may already own it." ;
    mem:tag "authority" ;
    mem:tag "contract" ;
    mem:tag "guarantee" ;
    mem:tag "openspec" ;
    mem:tag "review" ;
    mem:tag "search" ;
    mem:tag "trap" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:severity "should" ;
    mem:artifactRef "openspec/specs/runtime-harness-boundary/spec.md" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-11-18T18:11:43.261109+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:updatedAt "2026-11-18T19:41:14.930257+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "A review twice concluded a telemetry guarantee was only a test because searches covered READMEs, system docs and one phrasing; the accepted MUST sat in an openspec spec and the provider AGENTS.md." .

mem:constraint-01m8g09yspa7ecsny54kj43ys2 a mem:Constraint ;
    mem:content "The root bun run check schedules only each project's public check target; a project without one is never typechecked or policed by the repository gate, and nothing fails to report it. @habitat-ai/dev-service had no check target and sat outside the gate with a failing structure rule. Every non-root Nx project must declare check." ;
    mem:tag "check" ;
    mem:tag "dev-service" ;
    mem:tag "gate-hole" ;
    mem:tag "nx" ;
    mem:tag "scheduler" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:severity "must" ;
    mem:artifactRef "scripts/habitat/product-separation-absence.test.ts" ;
    mem:artifactRef "services/dev/project.json" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-11-28T02:38:47.094068+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

mem:decision-01m7qrnstmn6wwwvr0tc64dzp2 a mem:Decision ;
    mem:content "Habitat recovery uses one integrating director and a separate staffing-and-challenge director on the other runtime; the owner keeps product intent and admission of repairs and releases. Each working lane pairs a lead who owns the artifact with a lead on the other runtime who challenges it independently before the design is settled. A second runtime agreeing is not an independent verdict, and a director's agreement is not a method review. Current names, topics and routing live in the recovery workstream record, not here." ;
    mem:tag "agent-bus" ;
    mem:tag "claude" ;
    mem:tag "codex" ;
    mem:tag "coordination" ;
    mem:tag "directors" ;
    mem:tag "leads" ;
    mem:tag "recovery" ;
    mem:tag "staffing" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "docs/projects/habitat-sdk-recovery/triage.md" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-11-18T16:43:40.244600+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:updatedAt "2026-11-18T17:01:58.680146+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "Two runtimes work the recovery; one integrator avoids split direction while a separate staffing owner keeps independent challenge." ;
    mem:alternatives "single director for both runtimes,per-lane directors with no integrator" .

mem:decision-01m7qv68e9c53r97a16nwethmm a mem:Decision ;
    mem:content "Narsil is not the authority for symbol, reference, import or call edges in this repository. Verify any edge reported by its call-graph, import-graph, export-map and dependency tools in source, and do not read an absent edge as evidence that no relation exists. It may be used as an optional locator: reference and symbol-usage search with test exclusion, and plain-language hybrid search. Nx identifies the owning project and project dependencies; the TypeScript compiler resolves static symbols, types and imports; neither proves dynamic callbacks. Text location comes from ripgrep. Narsil's language-server mode and neural search were not evaluated." ;
    mem:tag "call-graph" ;
    mem:tag "code-intel" ;
    mem:tag "code-search" ;
    mem:tag "mcp" ;
    mem:tag "narsil" ;
    mem:tag "nx" ;
    mem:tag "tooling" ;
    mem:tag "typescript" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "AGENTS.md" ;
    mem:artifactRef "README.md" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-11-18T17:27:36.649465+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:updatedAt "2026-11-18T17:35:34.302744+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "Checked on two builds (a shared-daemon fork at 1.7.0 and stock 1.7.2) with the index verified current for the files asked about and the tool driven by its own usage guide, variants included. Direct same-module calls resolve. Optional and property calls are not edges; call targets resolve by bare name to test-file symbols even with test exclusion; re-export barrels have empty import and export maps; imported-by matches on basename and over-reports many times; top-level const initialisers have no caller symbol. Reference search with test exclusion and plain-language hybrid search do find candidate locations, inconsistently." ;
    mem:alternatives "keep Narsil as the declared symbol and reference authority,run it as a standing shared daemon for all agents,rely on its call graph with test exclusion" .

mem:decision-01m7r67jpsxdpye3tnqt6ha60s a mem:Decision ;
    mem:content "Owner-admitted terms for migrating Habitat from oRPC 2.0.0-beta.32 and Effect 4.0.0-beta.101 to beta.51 and 4.1.4: adopt the vendor's native results, not compatibility wrappers. A pending next during early stream return loses its value; unmapped declared error codes answer HTTP 400; declared errors end spans in ERROR. No SDK status-map option is promised: a surface that must keep an old status defers the upgrade. Admission covers the migration, its spec amendment, and landing it on main through the required check; it does not cover a release tag, publish, deploy or external export. One pack never certifies another: each candidate gets its own version and a full rerun on its own bytes. External telemetry export stays held by D-5; authored Effect middleware is unsupported." ;
    mem:tag "d-5" ;
    mem:tag "declared-error" ;
    mem:tag "effect" ;
    mem:tag "migration" ;
    mem:tag "orpc" ;
    mem:tag "owner-decision" ;
    mem:tag "stream-cancellation" ;
    mem:tag "upgrade" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "docs/projects/habitat-runtime-realignment/deferred-capabilities.md" ;
    mem:artifactRef "openspec/specs/runtime-harness-boundary/spec.md" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-11-18T20:40:34.265102+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:updatedAt "2026-11-22T23:04:49.038372+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "Design philosophy: vendors keep their semantics; a wrapper must earn its place. Packed and downstream evidence showed the native behaviour is coherent and the old results would need a Habitat shim or a second Effect runner." ;
    mem:alternatives "Hold the old cohort; add a public SDK error-status option; synthesize the trailing stream value; ban Effect middleware platform-wide" .

mem:decision-01m8g09yqkr5jyv6vzkccgaj7c a mem:Decision ;
    mem:content "Windows is parked from 0.7.0 by owner decision: not supported and not tested in CI. The installed-package acceptance matrix runs on Linux only and alone gates publication. The last full Windows run passed Habitat's Windows policy behaviour but stalled in workspace creation (over 180 s) and in bun install during an upgrade (over 120 s), cause unidentified. Resuming Windows means restoring its matrix entry and qualifying those setup paths; that is a separate owner decision." ;
    mem:tag "0.7.0" ;
    mem:tag "ci" ;
    mem:tag "owner-decision" ;
    mem:tag "parked" ;
    mem:tag "publish" ;
    mem:tag "release" ;
    mem:tag "windows" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef ".github/workflows/publish-habitat.yml" ;
    mem:artifactRef "apps/habitat/README.md" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-11-28T02:38:47.027788+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:updatedAt "2026-11-28T02:52:25.663277+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "The owner judged the Windows setup stall not worth further delay; the policy behaviour Habitat owns passes on hosted Windows while the stalls are in third-party install steps." ;
    mem:alternatives "hold the release until the full Windows suite is green,run the stall down on a disposable Windows machine first" .

mem:fact-01m7qsab9edfzxd3h6emtvsy07 a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "Habitat invocation continuation fails open: when the Effect fiber carries no continuation, assertAdmission falls back to assertOpen, which passes while the process is open. A lost effect/context lease therefore leaves ordinary oRPC traffic correct. Compatibility oracles for the oRPC-Effect bridge must also witness retained-view expiry or drain, and carry a marker through an authored Effect Context tag." ;
    mem:tag "bridge" ;
    mem:tag "compatibility-oracle" ;
    mem:tag "effect" ;
    mem:tag "effect-context" ;
    mem:tag "fail-open" ;
    mem:tag "invocation-continuation" ;
    mem:tag "orpc" ;
    mem:tag "process-runtime" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "packages/core/runtime/process-runtime/src/invocation-tracker.ts" ;
    mem:artifactRef "packages/core/runtime/process-runtime/src/server-request.ts" ;
    mem:artifactRef "packages/core/runtime/process-runtime/src/service-client-assembly.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-11-18T16:54:53.486247+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "Marker-only request tests stay green with the Effect lane dead, so they give false confidence in a dependency change." .

mem:fact-01m7qsabbk5rfgj5553gzc9680 a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "The Habitat SDK declares effect, @effect/opentelemetry and @orpc packages as exact dependencies, not peers, so a consumer's root versions or peer resolution cannot select the SDK's runtime cohort. A consumer can show candidate versions at top level while SDK dist and bridge import sites run the pinned cohort. Cohort qualification needs an SDK artifact built for that cohort, with versions resolved from the SDK dist and bridge import sites; name plus version does not identify the artifact." ;
    mem:tag "artifact-identity" ;
    mem:tag "cohort" ;
    mem:tag "effect" ;
    mem:tag "exact-dependencies" ;
    mem:tag "mixed-cohort" ;
    mem:tag "orpc" ;
    mem:tag "packed-consumer" ;
    mem:tag "peer-resolution" ;
    mem:tag "sdk" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "packages/core/sdk/package.json" ;
    mem:artifactRef "packages/core/sdk/tsdown.config.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-11-18T16:54:53.555599+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "A consumer-side override test can report the claimed versions while exercising a different or mixed runtime." .

mem:fact-01m7qsabdzp8tffg46vremcefh a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "The OpenTelemetry Node provider lazily imports its enabled module and turns any load failure into a degraded lease with PROVIDER_MODULE_LOAD_FAILED, so the process still starts and serves. A vendor export break can be silent at runtime when it gets past tsc. Dependency-compatibility checks that enable telemetry must assert exported oRPC spans and empty diagnostics, and treat a degraded provider as failure." ;
    mem:tag "PROVIDER_MODULE_LOAD_FAILED" ;
    mem:tag "degraded-lease" ;
    mem:tag "false-green" ;
    mem:tag "getOpenTelemetryConfig" ;
    mem:tag "opentelemetry" ;
    mem:tag "orpc" ;
    mem:tag "packed-consumer" ;
    mem:tag "telemetry" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "resources/telemetry/providers/opentelemetry-node/degraded.ts" ;
    mem:artifactRef "resources/telemetry/providers/opentelemetry-node/enabled.ts" ;
    mem:artifactRef "resources/telemetry/providers/opentelemetry-node/index.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-11-18T16:54:53.631135+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "Telemetry failure is contained by design, so a server smoke or request oracle cannot detect it." .

mem:fact-01m7qx2vmjhsdrtc7h8bwywvxz a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "oRPC tracer ownership trap for any upgrade past 2.0.0-beta.32. From upstream PRs 2000 and 2408 and a source reading of beta.51 (not runtime-verified): tracing moved behind a backend-neutral Tracer slot in @orpc/shared; getOpenTelemetryConfig is gone; ORPCInstrumentation.disable() clears any occupant of the slot and isEnabled() reports any occupant, by upstream design. Habitat's exact-owner release then depends on getTracer() identity, an exported but undocumented seam. A replacement-safety test must give the foreign instrumentation its own unregistered provider and assert export, not parentage. Reassess against the then-current release, not beta.51." ;
    mem:tag "beta" ;
    mem:tag "compatibility-trap" ;
    mem:tag "opentelemetry" ;
    mem:tag "orpc" ;
    mem:tag "ownership" ;
    mem:tag "telemetry" ;
    mem:tag "tracer" ;
    mem:tag "upgrade" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "resources/telemetry/providers/opentelemetry-node/enabled.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-11-18T18:00:42.386850+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

mem:fact-01m7qyd4b75cdebmz3ewy0g0jm a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "Habitat's authored Effect spans use the global OpenTelemetry tracer and active context through withNativeEffectTracing, so native oRPC spans do not prove authored tracing works. A host or instrumentation using a tracer provider that is not registered globally can export oRPC spans while habitat.runtime service spans are missing. To qualify a host-owned telemetry setup, require a habitat.runtime span under the native handler span; neither oRPC spans nor a degraded lease shows the host is healthy." ;
    mem:tag "borrowed-host" ;
    mem:tag "false-green" ;
    mem:tag "global-tracer" ;
    mem:tag "habitat.runtime" ;
    mem:tag "host-owned" ;
    mem:tag "opentelemetry" ;
    mem:tag "telemetry" ;
    mem:tag "tracer-provider" ;
    mem:tag "withNativeEffectTracing" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "packages/core/runtime/process-runtime/src/native-effect-tracing.ts" ;
    mem:artifactRef "resources/telemetry/providers/opentelemetry-node/AGENTS.md" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-11-18T18:23:47.559551+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "oRPC can use an injected provider while Habitat's Effect tracing reads the global API, so one healthy signal can hide the other being absent." .

mem:fact-01m7r2jdcj9gafak1dhjjw3e8x a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "Packed Habitat CLI/SDK candidates must not reuse a published version when installed from local tarballs. @habitat-ai/cli pins an exact @habitat-ai/sdk version, so Bun can satisfy the CLI's dependency from the registry and nest the published SDK with its old oRPC and Effect cohort beside the candidate root SDK. A symptom is '.effect is not a function'; commands that never reach .effect can pass. Use a unique version or a no-uplink registry, and require one SDK, one @orpc/server, one effect, and CLI-resolved SDK integrity equal to the candidate tarball." ;
    mem:tag "cli" ;
    mem:tag "effect-extension" ;
    mem:tag "false-green" ;
    mem:tag "orpc" ;
    mem:tag "packed-consumer" ;
    mem:tag "sdk" ;
    mem:tag "split-cohort" ;
    mem:tag "tarball-integrity" ;
    mem:tag "version-collision" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "apps/habitat/package.json" ;
    mem:artifactRef "apps/habitat/test/installed-package.test.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-11-18T19:36:34.962681+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

mem:fact-01m7r2jderbqm214hq8hwvtmas a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "oRPC Effect bridge error semantics differ across the upgrade: @orpc/experimental-effect 2.0.0-beta.32 handlerGen converts ORPCError to a success before effect/wrap and oRPC throws the returned error later, while @orpc/effect 2.0.0-beta.51 lets the failure pass through effect/wrap. From source reading, the wire response stays the same but Habitat's nativeEffect.typedFailure and authored server.operation/service.operation span status and exception events change. Upgrade checks need a declared-error case with telemetry, not only status and decoded data." ;
    mem:tag "beta.51" ;
    mem:tag "effect-bridge" ;
    mem:tag "effect-wrap" ;
    mem:tag "false-green" ;
    mem:tag "handlergen" ;
    mem:tag "orpc" ;
    mem:tag "orpcerror" ;
    mem:tag "span-status" ;
    mem:tag "typedfailure" ;
    mem:tag "upgrade" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "packages/core/runtime/process-runtime/src/native-effect-tracing.ts" ;
    mem:artifactRef "packages/core/runtime/process-runtime/src/server-request.ts" ;
    mem:artifactRef "packages/core/runtime/process-runtime/src/service-client-assembly.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-11-18T19:36:35.032839+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

mem:fact-01m7r2jdgnverrxcaff3bstqcg a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "The service blueprint's effect-bridge Grit rules match the oRPC Effect bridge package name literally, and the SDK ships those blueprints. Renaming the bridge without updating every blueprint version makes extension-placement and direct-bridge rules stop matching, while embedded examples using the old name can stay green. A bridge rename needs known-bad consumer controls using the new package name." ;
    mem:tag "blueprint" ;
    mem:tag "effect-bridge" ;
    mem:tag "experimental-effect" ;
    mem:tag "false-green" ;
    mem:tag "grit" ;
    mem:tag "orpc-effect" ;
    mem:tag "package-rename" ;
    mem:tag "policy" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef ".habitat/blueprints/service/components/funnel/effect-bridge.md" ;
    mem:artifactRef "packages/core/sdk/tsdown.config.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-11-18T19:36:35.093282+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

mem:fact-01m7r3hmzq0qfjem5kmvepsa3d a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "oRPC OpenAPI error status changes across the upgrade: a declared error code with no errorStatusMap entry returns HTTP 500 on 2.0.0-beta.32 and 400 on 2.0.0-beta.51 because DEFAULT_ERROR_STATUS changed, and the error body drops inferable. Common codes such as CONFLICT stay mapped (409). Habitat configures no errorStatusMap, so downstream apps inherit this; compare error-path responses, not only successful traffic, when qualifying the cohort." ;
    mem:tag "beta.51" ;
    mem:tag "declared-error" ;
    mem:tag "error-status" ;
    mem:tag "false-green" ;
    mem:tag "openapi" ;
    mem:tag "orpc" ;
    mem:tag "upgrade" ;
    mem:tag "wire" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "packages/core/runtime/process-runtime/src/server-request.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-11-18T19:53:38.551202+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

mem:fact-01m7r3hn22dm081wkvg88n8mn8 a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "@orpc/effect 2.0.0-beta.51 middlewareGen also calls effect/wrap, with kind middleware. Habitat's server wrap ignores kind, so on that cohort each Effect middleware adds a nested server.operation span and overwrites nativeEffect, outermost exit last. A handler Effect.die behind a pass-through middlewareGen was observed as typedFailure true, defect false, severity warning instead of defect true, severity error." ;
    mem:tag "beta.51" ;
    mem:tag "diagnostics" ;
    mem:tag "effect-wrap" ;
    mem:tag "middlewaregen" ;
    mem:tag "nativeeffect" ;
    mem:tag "orpc" ;
    mem:tag "server-operation" ;
    mem:tag "upgrade" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "packages/core/runtime/process-runtime/src/server-request.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-11-18T19:53:38.626857+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

mem:fact-01m7r3hn4a5wcc00t3na6s8hmc a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "Authored habitat.runtime spans (server.operation, service.operation) change status across the Effect 4.0.0-beta.101 to 4.1.4 cohort move: successful spans go from OK to UNSET, and with the oRPC beta.51 bridge a declared ORPCError goes from OK to ERROR with an exception event. Telemetry queries must not treat status OK as the success signal after this upgrade." ;
    mem:tag "authored-spans" ;
    mem:tag "effect" ;
    mem:tag "habitat-runtime" ;
    mem:tag "opentelemetry" ;
    mem:tag "span-status" ;
    mem:tag "upgrade" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "packages/core/runtime/process-runtime/src/native-effect-tracing.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-11-18T19:53:38.698311+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

mem:fact-01m7v877ytc6ct2mdrh977fkdh a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "The root bun run check schedules lint, typecheck, build and Habitat policy only; it runs no behaviour suites (stream closure, cleanup causes, middleware observation, telemetry provider, service command tests). A green check therefore says nothing about runtime behaviour. Qualifying a candidate source needs the focused bun and vitest suites replayed from a frozen clone of the exact commit, plus a falsification that removes each repair and shows its test fail." ;
    mem:tag "behaviour-tests" ;
    mem:tag "bun-run-check" ;
    mem:tag "false-green" ;
    mem:tag "focused-tests" ;
    mem:tag "frozen-clone" ;
    mem:tag "nx" ;
    mem:tag "qualification" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "package.json" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-11-20T01:13:03.706790+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

mem:fact-01m7v8780qc8s45skressbptz4 a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "The files at the service blueprint's kind root (.habitat/blueprints/service/README.md, skill.md, blueprint.toml, components/) are the immutable service@1 version, not editable unversioned guidance. Later versions live under versions/N. Stale wording there, such as a renamed vendor package, is fixed by routing authors of later versions to version-specific guidance, never by rewriting the root files." ;
    mem:tag "blueprint" ;
    mem:tag "guidance" ;
    mem:tag "immutable" ;
    mem:tag "readme" ;
    mem:tag "service" ;
    mem:tag "service-v1" ;
    mem:tag "skill" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef ".habitat/blueprints/service/README.md" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-11-20T01:13:03.767674+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

mem:fact-01m8g09yvqkgkc1d4ha1ywjb2p a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "In an uncached full check, TypeScript compilation is most of the Habitat task CPU and Grit a minority share concentrated in a few rules (the service Effect-bridge rule is several times slower than comparable rules). Machine saturation came from overlapping cold full runs, not Grit alone. The Grit provider's two-thread setting used about twice the CPU of one thread for the same wall time on the heaviest rules; lowering it needs a verdict-equality comparison first." ;
    mem:tag "check" ;
    mem:tag "cpu" ;
    mem:tag "grit" ;
    mem:tag "performance" ;
